exports[`keyrack github-app key on a box with no aws identity given: [case1] the blob lives only in aws.params (the clamp, red half) when: [t0] the box unlocks the key then: output matches snapshot 1`] = `
"🔓 keyrack unlock
   └─ @all.all.EHMPATH_BEAVER_GITHUB_TOKEN
      ├─ status: errored 💥
      └─ tip: aws.params found no AWS identity — fix: for --org @all run on a box whose instance role can read this param
         ├─ off ec2 (no instance role), for a github-app key, file its blob into os.secure on this box — from a box that can read the param, pipe it in: \`aws ssm get-parameter --name /keyrack/infra/vault/aws.params/v1/mechanic/_all_/all/EHMPATH_BEAVER_GITHUB_TOKEN --region us-east-1 --with-decryption --query Parameter.Value --output text | ssh <this box> rhx keyrack set --owner <owner> --key <full slug> --vault os.secure --mech EPHEMERAL_VIA_GITHUB_APP --source @stdin\`
         ├─ for a specific org, unlock that org's AWS_PROFILE first — run \`rhx keyrack unlock --owner <owner> --env <env>\` (declare the AWS_PROFILE key first if unset), never a cached SSO session
         └─ why (raw AWS): CredentialsProviderError — Could not load credentials from any providers"
`;

