exports[`keyrack github-app key on a box with no aws identity given: [case2] the blob is piped into os.secure (the clamp, green half) when: [t2] the box unlocks the key then: output matches snapshot 1`] = `
"🔓 keyrack unlock
   └─ @all.all.EHMPATH_BEAVER_GITHUB_TOKEN
      ├─ status: errored 💥
      └─ tip: failed to mint github app token — github refused the stored installation (404) — fix: the blob's appId or installationId names none github will serve: the app was uninstalled or suspended, the blob names another org, or its appId names no app. check the app's id and install, then re-file the current blob: <the current blob> | rhx keyrack set --owner mechanic --key @all.all.EHMPATH_BEAVER_GITHUB_TOKEN --vault os.secure --mech EPHEMERAL_VIA_GITHUB_APP --source @stdin
         └─ or, at a terminal with gh login, the guided set: rhx keyrack set --owner mechanic --key @all.all.EHMPATH_BEAVER_GITHUB_TOKEN --vault os.secure --mech EPHEMERAL_VIA_GITHUB_APP"
`;

